<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Marketplace standards</p><h1>Clear rules make a better market.</h1><p>These interim rules guide advertisers and buyers during the MC Exodus Market Place pilot.</p></div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="container narrow legal-copy">
    <p class="market-policy-date">Pilot policy · 13 November 2026</p>
    <h2>Advertising relationship</h2>
    <p>MC Exodus Market Place provides paid advertising space. Unless expressly stated otherwise, the platform does not own, inspect, deliver or guarantee advertised goods and is not a party to the private sale between a buyer and seller.</p>
    <h2>Advert approval</h2>
    <p>Every advert is subject to review. The team may request evidence of ownership, identity, pricing or product condition, and may reject or remove misleading, unsafe, unlawful or unsuitable content. Payment does not guarantee approval of prohibited content.</p>
    <h2>Prohibited advertising</h2>
    <p>Advertisers may not offer stolen or counterfeit goods, weapons, illegal substances, fake documents, exploitative content, unlicensed regulated products, fraudulent investments, or any product or service prohibited by Kenyan law.</p>
    <h2>Seller responsibilities</h2>
    <p>Sellers must provide accurate descriptions, current contact details, genuine photographs and a clear total price. Material defects, restrictions and relevant ownership information must be disclosed. Sellers are responsible for responding to enquiries and completing lawful transactions.</p>
    <h2>Buyer safety</h2>
    <p>Buyers should inspect products and ownership documents, meet in safe public locations, use traceable payment methods and obtain receipts. Never disclose passwords, PINs or one-time verification codes. Suspicious adverts should be reported to the marketplace team.</p>
    <h2>Payments, duration and refunds</h2>
    <p>Advertising charges cover publication for the selected duration and do not guarantee a sale or a specific number of enquiries. An advert rejected before publication will not be charged. Refund and correction decisions for an already published advert will be assessed according to the circumstances and the service delivered.</p>
    <h2>Personal information</h2>
    <p>Seller information is collected for advert review, communication, payment administration, fraud prevention and publication of approved contact details. Sellers should provide only information they are comfortable making public. Private review information will not be displayed as part of an advert.</p>
    <h2>Reporting and complaints</h2>
    <p>Concerns about an advert should identify the listing, the reason for the complaint and any supporting evidence. The marketplace team may temporarily hide an advert while reviewing a report.</p>
